Subject: [PATCH] aurora: name a touch of another enrolled finger as a plain no match

A single-finger verify (fprintd-verify with no -f picks the first enrolled
finger) accepts only the requested print. When the enclave matches another
enrolled finger of the same user, the driver reports no match, which is right,
but logged a warning that read like a print filed under the wrong identity.
Log it as what it is: the touch matched another enrolled print.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
diff --git a/libfprint/drivers/aurora/aurora.c b/libfprint/drivers/aurora/aurora.c
index c14db48..9d1cc33 100644
--- a/libfprint/drivers/aurora/aurora.c
+++ b/libfprint/drivers/aurora/aurora.c
@@ -1011,8 +1011,13 @@ aurora_verify_ready (gint fd, GIOCondition condition, gpointer user_data)
           else
             {
               aurora_uuid_hex (expected_uuid, expected_hex);
+              /* A single-finger verify accepts only the requested finger.
+               * A touch of another enrolled finger matches that finger's
+               * identity, and the answer is a plain no match: say so, so it
+               * does not read as a print filed under the wrong identity. */
               if (memcmp (expected_uuid, res.uuid, SEP_BIO_UUID_LEN) != 0)
-                g_warning ("SEP matched enclave identity %s; requested print identity is %s",
+                g_message ("the touch matched enclave identity %s, another enrolled print "
+                           "than the one requested (%s); reporting no match",
                            actual_hex, expected_hex);
               else
                 fp_dbg ("SEP matched requested enclave identity %s", actual_hex);
